# Wick — The assets this build produces

Wick ships with no pre-made art and no pre-made sound. This machine carries
asset tools on its `PATH`, and every sprite, sheet, icon, cue, and music bed
the game shows or plays is produced with them during this build, committed to
the repository, and bundled by it. This file is the contract: what to produce,
which tool produces it, where the file lands, and how the build reaches it.

Production is a one-time step. The tools belong to this machine and are absent
when the project is installed and rebuilt elsewhere, so the committed files are
the assets: `npm ci` and `npm run build` invoke no tool, and the built site
fetches nothing from outside its own `dist/`. A build that shells out to a
generation tool fails wherever the tools are absent, even though the game is
complete.

## The tools

| Tool | Produces | Used for |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `draw` | one sprite, a PNG | the still sprites: the idle lamplighter, the icons, the gems, the pickups, the ground tile, and the effects that hold one shape |
| `draw-sheet` | a sprite sheet, one PNG per frame | everything that moves on its own: the walk cycles, the death puff, and the animated effects |
| `sfx-synth` | a procedural sound, a `.wav` | the cues |
| `sfx-sample` | a sampled sound over a baked pack, a `.wav` | the cues, where a sampled layer suits one better |
| `music` | sequenced music over a baked instrument bank, a `.wav` and a `.mid` | the music bed |

Each is a command-line tool, and `<tool> --help` states its operations
(`<tool> <operation> --help` for one operation's flags). Each records the
operations run against it and then renders the finished file, which you commit
at the path this file names. `draw` and `draw-sheet` rasterize a fixed-size
RGBA canvas from drawing operations; `draw-sheet` takes a `--frame` on each
operation, so a sheet lands as separate files, one per frame, and it offers
layers with keyframes. `sfx-sample` draws on a baked sample pack and `music` on
a baked instrument bank, both browsed through their help; `music` emits a
portable `.mid` beside the `.wav`, and both are committed. Produce these files
with these tools; pre-made art, a downloaded sound, or a bundled font standing
in for a produced file does not meet this contract.

`particle-2d` is on the `PATH` as well. Wick plays no particle system, and any
flourish beyond the produced sprites is drawn in code.

## Where the files land, and how they are loaded

Every produced file sits under `assets/` at the root of this repository, at the
path named below, and is committed.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
The build loads them itself. Every URL it requests resolves against the page
rather than against the origin root, so the site runs unchanged whether it is
served from the root of a static host or mounted under a sub-path. A
root-absolute URL such as `/assets/sprites/ground.png` does not meet this: it
resolves against the origin and fails under a sub-path. Every image is decoded
and every sound is bound to its cue before the first frame draws.
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
The {{engine.name}} engine provides the asset loader and the audio cue bus,
both documented in the `engine/` directory at the root of this repository. The
loader resolves every path under one root, `assets/`, relative to the page the
build is served from, so the build asks it for a path written relative to that
root, such as `sprites/ground.png` and `audio/hit.wav`, rather than
constructing a URL of its own. Each image is loaded with `api.assets.loadImage`
and each audio cue below is bound to its produced file with `api.audio.load`
under its name in `CUES`, awaited in `initialize`, so every asset is decoded
before the first frame.
{{else}}
The {{engine.name}} engine provides the asset loader and the audio cue bus,
both documented in the `engine/` directory at the root of this repository. The
loader resolves every path under one root, `assets/`, relative to the page the
build is served from, so the build asks it for a path written relative to that
root, such as `sprites/ground.png` and `audio/hit.wav`, rather than
constructing a URL of its own. Each image is loaded with `api.assets.loadImage`
and each audio cue below is bound to its produced file with `api.audio.load`
under its name in `CUES`, awaited in the instance's `initialize`, so every
asset is decoded before the first frame.
{{/if}}

The simulation reads no image: a sprite's size in the world is the figure this
file states, and every hitbox is the shape `specs/weapons.md` and
`specs/enemies.md` give it, whatever the file decoded to. A load that fails
leaves the game running: the game still initializes, still ticks, still takes
input, and still draws a legible night when a sprite or a sound is unavailable,
so a missing file costs the game its polish rather than its playability.

## The sprites

Every sprite is pixel art drawn at one unit per pixel on a transparent,
straight-alpha canvas of exactly the size its row states, so a sprite `24`
pixels wide stands `24` units wide in the world, and the game draws it with
image smoothing off so it stays crisp at the stage's fit. Each is drawn
centered on the thing it depicts. A sheet's frames are separate PNG files,
numbered from `0`, each on a canvas of the sheet's size.

| Sprite | Files | Tool | Frames | Canvas |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Lamplighter, idle | `assets/sprites/lamplighter/idle.png` | `draw` | `1` | `24 x 32` |
| Lamplighter, walk | `assets/sprites/lamplighter/walk/0.png` to `5.png` | `draw-sheet` | `6` | `24 x 32` |
| Each common enemy, a walk cycle | `assets/sprites/enemies/<id>/0.png` to `3.png`, for each of the ten common ids in `ENEMY_IDS` | `draw-sheet` | `4` | twice its radius in `ENEMIES`, square: `20` for `moth`, `20` for `bat`, `24` for `rat`, `16` for `gnat`, `28` for `beetle`, `20` for `wisp`, `28` for `spider`, `24` for `crow`, `32` for `shade`, `36` for `hound` |
| Mothwing | `assets/sprites/enemies/mothwing/0.png` to `3.png` | `draw-sheet` | `4` | `56 x 56` |
| Owl | `assets/sprites/enemies/owl/0.png` to `3.png` | `draw-sheet` | `4` | `72 x 72` |
| The Dark | `assets/sprites/enemies/dark/0.png` to `3.png` | `draw-sheet` | `4` | `80 x 80` |
| Death puff, shared by every enemy | `assets/sprites/puff/0.png` to `3.png` | `draw-sheet` | `4` | `24 x 24` |
| Gems | `assets/sprites/gems/small.png`, `medium.png`, `large.png` | `draw` | `1` each | `8 x 8`, `12 x 12`, `16 x 16` |
| Pickups | `assets/sprites/pickups/chest.png`, `bread.png`, `draft.png` | `draw` | `1` each | `24 x 24` |
| Ground tile | `assets/sprites/ground.png` | `draw` | `1` | `64 x 64` |

Every enemy is told from every other at a glance, by silhouette and not by hue
alone, and the two elites and the Dark read as larger and heavier than the
commons. The three gem tiers are told apart by size and form. The ground tile
sits flush against itself on all four sides, since the ground is that tile
repeated across the world.

### The weapon effects

Each weapon has one effect the game draws wherever the weapon's shape is live,
as `specs/weapons.md` and `specs/evolutions.md` define that shape. Each is
produced on the canvas its row states and scaled in code to the live shape,
which `areaMul` and later levels grow, so the effect's drawn extent is the
hitbox's extent on every tick it is drawn.

| Effect | Weapon | Files | Form | Canvas | Drawn over |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| slash | Taper | `assets/sprites/effects/taper.png` | one sprite | `120 x 40` | the `width x height` rectangle, for `SLASH_FLASH` (`0.1`) seconds |
| bolt | Ember | `assets/sprites/effects/ember.png` | one sprite | `16 x 16` | the bolt's circle, for its life |
| dart | Pin | `assets/sprites/effects/pin.png` | one sprite | `12 x 12` | the dart's circle, for its life |
| lantern | Lantern | `assets/sprites/effects/lantern.png` | one sprite | `28 x 28` | each lantern's circle, for its life |
| aura ring | Halo | `assets/sprites/effects/halo.png` | one sprite, a ring | `160 x 160` | the aura's circle, always, with its pulse readable |
| puddle | Oil Splash | `assets/sprites/effects/oil-splash.png` | one sprite | `100 x 100` | the puddle's circle, for its life |
| strike | Spark | `assets/sprites/effects/spark/0.png` to `3.png` | a sheet of `4`, played once | `80 x 80` | the strike's `area` circle, for `SPARK_FLASH` (`0.2`) seconds |
| shard | Shard | `assets/sprites/effects/shard.png` | one sprite | `16 x 16` | the shard's circle, for its life |
| sconce | Sconce | `assets/sprites/effects/sconce/0.png` to `3.png` | a sheet of `4`, spinning | `24 x 24` | the sconce's circle, for its life |
| flare burst | Flare | `assets/sprites/effects/flare/0.png` to `5.png` | a sheet of `6`, played once | `128 x 128` | the burst's circle, for `FLARE_FLASH` (`0.4`) seconds |

