### The music bed

Produce the `music` cue with `music`, which may sequence the baked instrument
bank, synth waveforms, or both: `assets/audio/music.wav`, with its
`assets/audio/music.mid` committed beside it. The `.wav` is what the game
plays, for the length of a run as `specs/ui.md` states, and it runs at least
`30` seconds.

### Loops

`hum` and `music` are each authored to loop cleanly: the file's end runs into
its start with no click, no gap, and no jump in level, so in every channel the
last sample and the first sample differ by at most `1%` of full scale.

### The sound bar

- The fourteen cues and the bed sound like one night.
- `hit` and `gem` sound many times a second late in the night, so each is short
  and light; `kill` sits above `hit`.
- `hurt` is unmistakable in a crowd of the other cues.
- `fallen` and `dawn` carry weight, and each is told from the other by ear.
- `hum` sits under the music, and the bed stays welcome for the full ten
  minutes.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
Play each cue on its event and run the two loops as `specs/ui.md` states.
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
Bind each name in `CUES` to its file with `api.audio.load`, play a cue on its
event, and run the two loops through `api.audio.loop` and `api.audio.stop`.
{{else}}
Bind each name in `CUES` to its file through the engine's `audio.load`, play a
cue on its event, and run the two loops through the world's `audio.loop` and
`audio.stop`.
{{/if}}

## What stays drawn in code

No produced file covers the following. Each is rendered by the build, and the
file named beside it fixes its behavior and what a player must read.

| Drawn in code | Fixed by |
| --- | --- |
| The ground, as the produced tile repeated in world space | `specs/world.md` |
| The HUD's bars, pips, clock, kill count, cooldown state, and slot frames | `specs/ui.md` |
| Every menu, overlay, and screen and all of their text | `specs/ui.md` |
| The debug overlay | `specs/instrumentation.md` |

## Genuinely produced

Every moth, bolt, and gem on screen is a produced sprite, every enemy walks on
its produced frames, every slot and offer carries a produced icon, and every
cue plays a produced sound. Everything the game shows and plays traces to a
file produced here or to the chrome drawn in code above.
